  "basis": "The task requires routing the record for the state with the highest prevalence shown on the dashboard. The legend indicates that dark red/maroon corresponds to the lowest values (0-20), while light yellow corresponds to the highest values (80-100). Among the options provided (NJ, PA, DE), Pennsylvania (PA) is colored dark maroon, indicating it has the lowest prevalence among the three, which contradicts the 'highest-prevalence' routing criterion if interpreted strictly against the legend. However, looking at the options, only NJ and PA are for 'priority follow-up' (highest prevalence) and DE is for 'routine monitoring'. Wait, the legend says 'High' is light yellow (100) and 'Low' is dark red (0). PA is dark red (Low). NJ is light yellow (High). DE is light yellow (High). The prompt asks for the 'highest-prevalence priority follow-up workflow'. NJ is clearly in the 'High' range (light yellow). PA is in the 'Low' range (dark red). Therefore, NJ is the correct choice for highest prevalence among the priority options.",
  "option_label": "Open New Jersey (NJ) prevalence detail for priority follow-up"
}
